    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        40,
        1000
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        700
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax-H3 all-in-one (H3-06)\nOne entry graph for the three H3 modes. Each mode is a group; only **T2VA** is active by default and the other groups are muted.\n\n**Switch mode:** right-click a group title and choose *Set Group Nodes to Always*, then set the other mode groups to *Never*. You can also select nodes and press **Ctrl+M** to mute/unmute them. Keep exactly one mode group active unless you want several results in one run.\n\n| Mode | Connect | Server task |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| T2VA | prompt only | `t2va` |\n| FL2VA | first frame, last frame, or both | `fl2va` |\n| Ref2VA | images / videos / audio via Video References | `ref2va` |\n\n**Shared settings** (server URL, served model name, duration, sampling, flow shifts) feed every mode. A combined H3 service started without `--task-type` serves all three modes; an FL2VA-only service serves T2VA and FL2VA. See `docs/h3-06-all-in-one.md`.\n\nDuration 5.167 s at 24 FPS = 124 frames (H3 needs `17k+5`). Width/height select the T2VA aspect ratio; FL2VA and Ref2VA take it from the inputs.\n\nWrite each mode's own prompt, including its sound. This graph has **no prompt-assistance stage**: H3 does not supply a prompt LLM."
      ],
      "title": "How to use this graph"
    },
